{"ts":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"87347b071d1305e7d9cbbd27","agent_provenance":{"model":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-fqdmbf"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-803: hoist repeated linked-test execution context and honor lean output"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm test --run --json repeats a 16-field sandbox execution_context on every result even though the context is invocation-scoped; in the reported one-test case it consumes 727 of 1,301 bytes and grows redundantly with each linked test."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:sdk","context-management","gh-issue","linked-tests","output-contract","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Invocation-scoped execution context is emitted once rather than duplicated on every linked-test result, with no diagnostic information loss; Lean structured output omits non-actionable successful-run sandbox plumbing while failures retain enough provenance to diagnose context isolation; Default and full projections remain explicitly contracted and backward compatibility is handled through a documented schema/version strategy; CLI, SDK, MCP, JSON schemas, contracts, and documentation expose one consistent test-run output shape; Measured multi-test output proves a material byte and token reduction while focused and exact 100 percent coverage remain green"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Pay once for invocation provenance and reserve per-result output for result-specific evidence"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents retain more context for actionable test failures and project decisions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Removes multiplicative payload overhead from linked-test sweeps without discarding sandbox diagnostics"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Structured linked-test output scales with useful results rather than repeated temporary-path plumbing"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"GH-803 measured execution_context at 56 percent of a passing one-test JSON response and identified per-result duplication that worsens with fleet sweeps"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Enable test-result-tracking in a fresh workspace, link multiple passing tests, run pm test --run --json, and compare repeated execution_context bytes with result-specific bytes."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"One invocation-level execution context plus compact result-specific records, with lean success output and diagnostic failure output."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Every result repeats the same 16-field sandbox context, including temporary absolute paths, regardless of status or lean intent."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.7.29"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"linked-test-output-contract"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Fleet-wide linked-test sweeps spend most structured output on repeated sandbox plumbing that cannot change an agent decision."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-cxr0jb","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-g3n00m","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-oi4zs3","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vrsn","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for execution_context, sandbox plumbing, lean output, and GH-778 found closed pm-oi4zs3 for caller echoes and inactive pagination metadata plus open pm-5t33or/pm-cxr0jb for general budget and intent projections. None owns invocation-level hoisting or status-aware linked-test provenance, so GH-803 is a distinct successor in that canonical lineage: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/803."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9e82f62280d2b8b32836e9f8f2723144a504de7732fffcc462256d66732bdd60","message":"Track GH-803 linked-test context efficiency"}
